! A beam with no vertical size (emit_y = 0), so y is exactly 0 and Faddeeva::w takes its real-axis branch
! (w_im's table, copied unchanged), and a second element 0.2 mm off in x. Rounding expected
Q1: QUAD, L=0.1, K1=0.5
D: DRIF, L=0.2
BB: BEAMBEAM, CHARGE=5e-9, XSIZE=80e-6, YSIZE=20e-6
BB2: BEAMBEAM, CHARGE=5e-9, XSIZE=80e-6, YSIZE=20e-6, XCENTER=2e-4
BL: LINE=(Q1, D, BB, D, BB2, D)
